<article class="env-proposition" id="04FA">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04FA">Proposition <span data-tag="04FA">8.6.7.2</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be a locally Kan simplicial category. Then: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}^{\asymp }$ of Notation <a data-tag="04F9" href="/tag/04F9">8.6.7.1</a> is locally Kan. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The forgetful functor $\pi : \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}^{\asymp } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is a weak equivalence of simplicial categories (see Definition <a data-tag="01Q0" href="/tag/01Q0">4.8.4.8</a>). 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(3)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The functor $\pi $ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}^{\asymp } ) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assertions $(1)$ and $(2)$ follow immediately from Corollary <a data-tag="048J" href="/tag/048J">8.1.2.3</a>; assertion $(3)$ then follows from Corollary <a data-tag="01Q1" href="/tag/01Q1">4.8.4.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
